  "confidence_note": "The Western convention set out under Shoghi Effendi (Naw-Rúz on 21 March, the Twin Holy Days on 20 October and 12 November), as kept in the West. Bahá’ís in Iran reckoned differently: see eastern_reconstruction and https://lessan.github.io/bahai-date/history.html.",
  "eastern_reconstruction_note": "For 1-171 B.E.: Naw-Rúz by the rule used from 172 B.E. (the day, sunset to sunset in Ṭihrán, in which the March equinox falls), applied backwards, and the length of Ayyám-i-Há that follows from it. A modern reconstruction, not a record of what any community observed; uncertain where the equinox falls within 15 minutes of sunset. Bahá’ís in Iran also kept the Twin Holy Days, the Declaration and the Martyrdom of the Báb on Islamic lunar dates, which are not given here.",
